WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:30.080
Open a weekly-pack request for the synthetic sales data.

2
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:36.920
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the sales manager: requests the pack.

3
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:40.400
Save the request to start the workflow.

4
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:58.320
The workflow calculates figures, checks the summary and holds the pack for review.

5
00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:35.360
The held pack keeps its summary and the exact version for review.

6
00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:43.560
Code calculates chart values and checks figures in the AI-written summary.

7
00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:13.040
Open a decision for the exact pack version being reviewed.

8
00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:21.640
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the sales manager: records this version's approval.

9
00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:25.120
Save the decision with the pack version.

10
00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:36.120
The workflow checks the decision and releases the approved pack.

11
00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:08.100
The approved version lands once on the demo email board.

12
00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:31.480
Open InsightsIQ, iMBrace's analysis workspace, and choose the sales chart assistant.

13
00:03:31.480 --> 00:04:53.320
Ask for a sales chart using the fictional distributor's records.

14
00:04:53.400 --> 00:05:01.800
InsightsIQ draws the requested chart from totals returned by the read-only skill.

15
00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:27.480
The read-only skill checks this request against its allowed actions.

16
00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:38.160
The skill keeps synthetic sales records available for analysis.

17
00:05:42.120 --> 00:06:01.360
Open DataIQ, iMBrace's records workspace, to inspect the source data.

18
00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:11.200
The fictional distributor's latest-week sales records remain available for analysis.
